            <div xml:id="d591">

                <pb facs="0635" n="621" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg621"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.61333/955: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-03-25T15:00:00-03:00">March 25, 1944—3
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 5:32 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1135. Embassy’s telegram 1047, March 20, 7 p.m.<anchor n="87" xml:id="d591-f1"/>
                    The Minister of Finance has agreed to recommend to President Vargas termination
                    of the coffee agreement and the ship deal. The latter was referred to him
                    because of its connection with the coffee transaction. He promised to send the
                    papers to the Foreign Office and President Vargas next week.</p>
                <p>Both the Minister of Finance and Penteado, who is scheduled to arrive in
                    Washington within a few days, are greatly concerned over a probable increase in
                    coffee quotas.…</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
